INT. STALLED ELEVATOR, GRANDVIEW HOTEL - DAY

A mirrored box, brass rails. A tiered wedding cake in a white box sits on a luggage cart in the center. The floor indicator is stuck between 14 and 15.

BARTHOLOMEW "BART" KWIATKOWSKI, fifties, pastry chef in whites, grips the cart with both hands. YOLANDA PRICE, thirties, the wedding planner, in a headset and heels, stabs the alarm button. CHEN WEI, twenties, the bellhop, leans against the rail eating a granola bar. FIONNUALA DOYLE, sixties, the bride's grandmother, sits on a folding stool she has brought from somewhere, knitting.

                    YOLANDA
          Okay. Everyone remain calm.

                    BART
          I am calm. This cake is not calm.

                    CHEN
          It's a cake.

                    BART
          It is forty-eight hours of fondant.

The elevator shudders. The cake tiers slide an inch. Bart and Yolanda lunge at the same time and bump foreheads.

                    YOLANDA
          Ow!

                    BART
          Ow!

Fionnuala keeps knitting.

                    FIONNUALA
          Always the same with the young. You rush and then you bleed.

                    YOLANDA
          (muttering)
          The ceremony starts in thirty minutes.

                    CHEN
          I can call someone.

                    YOLANDA
          Please do.

He pulls a walkie-talkie from his belt, presses the key, and hears only static. He taps it against his palm. Bart watches the cake like a man watching a cliff.

                    BART
          (to himself)
          Don't tilt. Don't tilt.

                    FIONNUALA
          Chen, dear, is there a phone number on the wall?

                    CHEN
          Yes, ma'am.

                    FIONNUALA
          Then why on earth aren't we using it?

Everyone turns to the wall. A small door in the panel reads EMERGENCY PHONE. Yolanda yanks it open. Inside is a handset and a sticker: OUT OF ORDER.

                    YOLANDA
          Of course.

The elevator drops two inches. The cake slides. Bart and Chen and Yolanda all dive for it, and the three of them end up in a pile on top of the cart, holding the box together like a family hugging.

Fionnuala turns a row on her needles and does not look up.

                    FIONNUALA
          Well. That's one way to do it.
